From 91b99685f8b7a165a9afeea38b4b75ce7906e00b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sacha Gavino <sacha.gavino@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 15:31:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Guard the derived grid path with a bit-identical
 round-trip test

The stage-2 equivalence test only exercises the *tabulated* grid path: its
reference is nmgc-2.0's 2-bin, ~8-mass-decade grid, which no mass_ratio<=2
derivation can reproduce. The derived path became the default at stage 3 and
had no automated guard. It has one now.

tests/roundtrip_derived.sh runs a derived + MRN grid, feeds that run's
dust_grid_active.out export back in as dust_grid_table.in with
dust_grid_source=tabulated / dust_ic=tabulated and every other input held
fixed, and requires abundances.out to be byte-identical between the two.
This proves get_grain_radii() fills the same per-bin arrays whether they come
from the derivation or the tabulated reader, and that the chemistry consumes
them identically.

- Self-contained: needs no external nmgc-2.0 binary, unlike equivalence.sh,
  so it can run in CI. ~70 s including the build.
- Uses a 4-bin grid on purpose (a_max clipped, mass_ratio still 2): bin count
  changes only the species count and hence the runtime, never which code paths
  are taken, and grain-surface species are template-replicated per bin so a
  20-bin science grid is slow until the stage-4 RHS work lands. Grid and run
  length are overridable from the environment (RT_AMIN/RT_AMAX/RT_STOP/...).
- On failure it converts to ASCII and reports the worst per-species relative
  difference, skipping gas_phase.ab (species-name column) as equivalence.sh does.

Verified: passes byte-identical on abundances.out and elemental_abundances.out
at both -O0 and -O2. Confirmed the guard is not inert: feeding back a table
truncated to 14 significant figures makes it fail (worst relative difference
4.2e-2, on a trace species near the network floor), which is the ~1e-13
input-perturbation amplification docs/STAGE3_GRID.md already describes.
